>Also, can someone describe what an athame looks like?

(Wow!  Finally a question I'm qualified to answer!!)  >8->

It's a ceremonial knife in Wicca and some other magical traditions.
USUALLY a black handled, double-edged dagger, though I've seen many
variants.  (My own started as all-black, and has since been polished to
mostly-silver.)  It's used in ritual for directing energy and casting
Circles, and is the representative tool for Air or Fire, depending on whom
you ask.  Some people believe that the athame should ONLY be used for ritual
and should never be used to cut organic matter; others follow the "kitchen
magic" approach and think that the more uses you put your athame to, the
better.  (I think we can all guess where the average NetHack wizard stands
on the issue.)  >8->    Swords are sometimes used for the same purpose,
though they're rarely called athames.  

BTW, if I remember right, there's a description in the NetHack data file 
for it.  Put your athame down and use "/" to look at it, or just type
"/nathame".

